<para id="RM0000016A3010X" category="J" type-id="8010W" name-id="652MJ-00" from="200612" to="200912">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>A "beep" sounds when the voice recognition switch is pressed, but voice cannot be recognized</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000016A3010X_01" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AE500000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E147223J01" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000016A3010X_02" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AE600000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When replacing the navigation receiver assembly on a vehicle not subscribed to the G-BOOK service, perform the vehicle linking setting. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000001C3S00RX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When replacing the navigation receiver assembly on a vehicle subscribed to the G-BOOK service, perform the vehicle linking setting, then perform the G-BOOK use resumption operation and HELPNET service start operation. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM000001C3S00RX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the navigation receiver assembly is replaced while a purchased G-SOUND unlimited license exists, perform G-SOUND license recovery. (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM000001C3S00RX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM0000016A3010X_03" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A3010X_03_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AE700000">
<testtitle>Start Diagnosis</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the procedure, see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000002RV02BX"/></ptxt>
</atten4>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0002" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A3010X_03_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AE800000">
<testtitle>Microphone Check (Microphone Input Level)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Microphone Check (Microphone Input Level)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E122002" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Select "Navigation Check" on the diagnosis check menu screen to display the navigation check menu screen.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Select "Microphone &amp; Voice Recognition Check" on the Navigation &amp; Check Menu screen to display the microphone voice recognition check screen.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Speak into the microphone and inspect the display of the microphone input level gauge.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Microphone input level gauge moves</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0003" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0004" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A3010X_03_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AE900000">
<testtitle>Microphone Check (Recording and Playback of Spoken Voice)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Microphone Check (Recording and Playback of Spoken Voice)</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E122002" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>After pressing the record switch, speak into the microphone and record the voice.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Press the playback switch and check the recorded voice.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>The spoken voice is played back normally without noise, distortion, etc.</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>During playback of the recorded voice, the microphone input level gauge does not respond to the playback sound.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The content spoken during recording is optional.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Recording stops after 5 seconds elapse or when the stop switch is pressed.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>During recording and playback, all switch operations except the stop switch are disabled.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When nothing has been recorded, the playback switch is grayed out.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Playback ends when playback of the recorded content is finished.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0014" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0004" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A3010X_03_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AEB00000">
<testtitle>Re-operate (Voice Recognition)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Re-operate (Voice Recognition)</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Pay attention to how you speak and perform the voice recognition operation again.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Voice is recognized normally</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When recognized normally, a talk-back is given.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If unnecessary words ("er", "um", etc.) are added before or after the recognition word, it will be misrecognized.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Voices cannot be recognized if several people speak at the same time.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the speaking speed is extremely fast or slow, the recognition rate may drop significantly.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Recognition may be difficult depending on voice quality. (Hoarse voice due to poor health, etc.)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0009" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM0000016A3010X_03_0010" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM0000016A3010X_03_0009">
<testtitle>Normal (voice recognition may be difficult depending on how the user speaks)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
